.Dd October 19, 2026
.Dt IMP72STAGE0 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm imp72stage0
.Nd compile IMP72 programs to native code
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl C
.Op Fl S | Fl c
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Op Fl s Ar letters
.Ar file.imp ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
compiles programs in IMP72, the extensible systems language of Ned Irons as
implemented by Walter Bilofsky for the PDP-10 (DECUS 10-198a), to native code.
The syntax of the language is read from the original syntax file
.Pa syntax.imc .
The compiler's code generator makes PDP-10 code, which is translated to an
intermediate form and from there to machine code.
.Pp
IMP72 passes arguments by reference, as FORTRAN does, and a word is 64 bits
(32 bit hosts hold it in a
.Vt long long ) .
A subroutine
.Sy SUBR
is therefore a C function of pointers to its arguments, returning a word,
and a C program can call it.
.Sy CCALL F(A, B)
calls the C function
.Fn F
with the values of
.Va A
and
.Va B .
Variables are common symbols.
.Pp
Unless told otherwise,
.Nm
compiles with the code generator of pcc where it was built
.Pq amd64, aarch64 and i386 hosts
and with the host's C compiler elsewhere.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl C
Use the C back end: the program is turned into C and compiled by the host's
C compiler.
This is the only back end on hosts that pcc does not build for.
.It Fl S
Stop after generating assembly
.Pq with Fl C , No C .
.It Fl c
Stop after generating the object file.
.It Fl o Ar output
Name of the output file.
.It Fl s Ar letters
Switches for the compiler proper: listings and dumps of its tables, as in the
original.
.Ql A
assembly listing,
.Ql T
code tree,
.Ql S
semantics,
.Ql X
syntax graph.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev IMP72BACKEND
.Ql c
or
.Ql pcc ,
to choose the back end.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/share/imp72/syntax.imc
The syntax of IMP72.
.It Pa /usr/share/imp72/ffi.imc
The extension that adds
.Sy CCALL .
.It Pa /usr/lib/imp72/
The compiler proper, the back ends and the runtime library
.Pa libimp72.a .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cc 1 ,
.Xr pcc 1
.Pp
.Pa /usr/share/doc/imp72/
.Sh AUTHORS
The original IMP72 is by
.An Walter Bilofsky ;
the IMP language by
.An Ned Irons .
